]]\n*[[Cookbook:Chopping|Chopped]] [[Cookbook:parsley|parsley]]\n*[[Cookbook:salt|Salt]]\n*[[Cookbook:nutmeg|Nutmeg]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:flour|flour]]\n*1 tbsp grated [[Cookbook:Parmesan Cheese|Parmesan cheese]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Soak the breadcrumbs in a little stock.\n# Combine the butter, eggs, soaked breadcrumbs, a little chopped parsley, salt, and a [[Cookbook:pinch|pinch]] of nutmeg.\n# Reduce this,{{Clarify|reason=How do you cook this until thicker, without cooking the eggs and thus making it impossible to stir in the flour and cheese?}} then add flour and Parmesan cheese.\n#Form this mixture into little [[Cookbook:Quenelle|quenelles]], and [[Cookbook:boiling|boil]] them in stock for a few minutes.\n#Put them into a tureen and pour a good clear soup over them.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread crumb]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using parsley]]\n[[Category:Recipes using nutmeg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using broth and stock]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Roman Soup","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 oz (115 g) breadcrumbs","sourceText":"4 oz (115 g) breadcrumbs","amountText":"4 oz (115 g) breadcrumbs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Stock","sourceText":"Stock","amountText":"Stock","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"3.5 oz (100 g) butter","sourceText":"3.5 oz (100 g) butter","amountText":"3.5 oz (100 g) butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 eggs","sourceText":"2 eggs","amountText":"2 eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Chopped parsley","sourceText":"Chopped parsley","amountText":"Chopped parsley","amount":null,"unit":null